app orb-goldens-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for `orb goldens <file.goldens.json>`: the parity-golden replay. A golden file names an atom (path under the std lolo root, resolved two directories above the file's topic folder), a default trait and cases; each case is a list of steps {trait?, from?, event, payload, expect {fired?, state?, emits?, neverEmits?, effects?} (effects: the step's reported effects, matched in order by type, status, routed and key, where key is the options map at args[optionsAt], default 2; argN compares the whole unevaluated argument N)} played through the kernel in ONE program/step call (a fresh kernel per case). It prints one `pass` or `fail` line per case (the failed expectations after it), then `N passed, M failed`; exit 0 when none failed and one passed, 1 otherwise, 2 on a usage error. A directory argument (anything not ending in .goldens.json) replays every *.replay.goldens.json in it, sorted, and totals the cases. A case may carry skip (a reason: printed as `skip`, counted apart, never a failure), entity and now (entity seeds the first step and a step may carry its own entity; a step now overrides) and config (unsupported until G-ORB-460: it fails the case); any other case, step or expect key fails the case, and so does expect.entity (program/step answers no post-step entity row), and a step may carry keep + keepField: after the step the first emitted payload holding keepField is stored under keep and a later step payload value written as a dollar sign followed by the keep name is replaced by it (the prefix of steps is replayed each time, so the kernel stays deterministic). Runner limits: an expected emit matches an emitted event in order, not necessarily adjacent, by event name and by every payload key it names, each key compared whole-value (structurally, objects order-insensitive), so a nested expected object must equal the actual, not be a subset of it; cascaded traits' emits are not seen (program/step reports the first outcome only)."
]

orbital OrbGoldensSpec {
  expects trait OrbGoldens {
    state ready
    emits {
      GOLDENS_ANSWERED { status : number!  body : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page "/orb-goldens" -> OrbGoldens
}
